= AYON Publish ROP =

#icon: opdef:/ayon::Driver/ayon_publish::1.0?AYON_icon.png

"""Publishes the output of connected ROPs as a single AYON product."""

== Overview ==

The AYON Publish ROP is a generic publish node for the `/out` context. Connect
one or more ROPs that write files to it; each input ROP becomes a
representation of the published product. This works with standard Houdini ROPs,
custom studio ROPs and cache nodes such as [Node:out/filecache].

Set the AYON `Folder Path`, `Task Name`, `Variant` and `Product Type` on the
node. The folder, task and variant controls have picker buttons; the product
type menu lists the common AYON product types. Publish by rendering the AYON
Publish ROP, or create a publish instance from the node in the Publisher UI.

The latest publish report is kept on the node as cached data (not saved with
the hip file); use **Save Publish Report...** or **Copy Publish Report** at the
bottom of the parameters to inspect it.

Full documentation:
https://github.com/ynput/ayon-houdini/blob/develop/docs/publish-rop.md

== Parameters ==

@parameters

Folder Path:
    AYON folder to publish into. Use the picker button to choose from the
    current project's folders.
Task Name:
    Task of the folder. Use the picker button to choose from the folder's
    tasks.
Variant:
    Product variant. The picker lists the creator's default variants and the
    variants already used by AYON Publish ROPs in the scene.
Product Type:
    AYON product type; defaults to `rop_publish`.
Active:
    When off, publishing this node is skipped.
Save Publish Report...:
    Save the last publish report of this node to a JSON file.
Copy Publish Report:
    Copy the last publish report of this node to the clipboard.

@related

* [Node:out/rop]
* [Node:out/filecache]
* [https://github.com/ynput/ayon-houdini/blob/develop/docs/publish-rop.md]
